      "quote": "Conversely, suppose $x>a_1$ belongs to $S$. Because the sequence is strictly increasing, it is unbounded. Choose the unique $n$ for which $a_n<x\\le a_{n+1}$. Since $x\\in S$, it has gcd greater than 1 with each of $a_1,\\ldots,a_n$. The minimality in the definition of $a_{n+1}$ therefore gives $a_{n+1}\\le x$. Hence $x=a_{n+1}$.",
