      "quote": "If a family of finite sets is pairwise intersecting and has a member $C$ of size $r$, then it has only finitely many inclusion-minimal finite transversals.",
      "note": "This general lemma is false (e.g. F_k={x_1,...,x_k,y_k} is pairwise intersecting with infinitely many minimal transversals); the tree argument is invalid, and no large-prime erasure is ever given."
